A survey of 1,400 people prior to the 2010 federal election found that the number of opponents of the transformation from Australia to the Republic had increased by 8% since 2008.
Interim Prime Minister Julia Gillard said during the 2010 federal election campaign that she believed Australia should become a republic at the end of the reign of Queen Elizabeth II.
34% of respondents share this view, and want Queen Elizabeth II to be the last monarch to rule over Australia.
At the extremes of the survey, 29% of respondents believe that Australia should become a republic as quickly as possible, while 31% believe that Australia should never become a republic.
