If you’ve seen the movie Benjamin Gates and the Templar Treasure, you might think a treasure map was drawn on the back of the Declaration of Independence.
However, that's not true. Although there's an inscription on the back of the document, it's not a treasure map.
On the back of the Declaration of Independence read the words "Original Declaration of Independence dated 4 July 1776". The text is at the bottom of the document.
Although no one really knows who wrote it, it is known that at an early stage of its existence, the large parchment (which measures about 29 inches three-quarters by 24 inches) was stored rolled.
It is therefore likely that the notation has been added simply as a label.
