Ancient China had a unique way of showing the different eras; every stage of China or every family that was in power was a separate dynasty.
Between each dynasty, there was also an unstable age of divided provinces. The most well-knowned of these periods is the era of the Three Kingdoms which took place for 60 years between the Han Dynasty and the Jin Dynasty.
During these periods, ferocious struggles took place between many members of the nobility fighting for the throne.
The Three Kingdoms were one of the most bloodthirsty eras in the history of Chinese antiquity. Thousands of people died in battle to sit on the throne of the great palace of XI'an.
